    {
      "title": "Backups and Recovery: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Backups and Recovery: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Backup Types and Restore Chains",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Copies",
                "Restore needs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Full**",
                  "everything",
                  "full only"
                ],
                [
                  "**Differential**",
                  "changes since last {blue:full}",
                  "full + differential (2 sets)"
                ],
                [
                  "**Incremental**",
                  "changes since last backup of {orange:any type}",
                  "full + every incremental, in order (longest, {red:most fragile})"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Incremental}: smallest and fastest backup, ==slowest restore==",
                "{blue:Differential}: grows daily, restores with ==just 2 sets=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Logical vs Physical",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Logical",
                "Physical"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "`pg_dump`, `mysqldump`",
                  "file / block copy"
                ],
                [
                  "Content",
                  "SQL text",
                  "raw data files"
                ],
                [
                  "Portable",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:same version and platform}"
                ],
                [
                  "Restore",
                  "{red:slow}",
                  "{green:fast}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. RPO and RTO",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RPO== = how much data you can lose",
                "==RTO== = how long you can be down",
                "Both decide the **backup frequency** and the **tools** you pick"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pick by the targets",
              "text": "A tight ==RPO== needs frequent backups. A tight ==RTO== needs fast restores: **physical** copies and short restore chains."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "WAL, Checkpoints and Point-in-Time Recovery",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "WAL, Checkpoints and Point-in-Time Recovery",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Write-Ahead Logging",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==WAL rule==: the log record hits durable disk **before** the changed data page",
                "{green:Commit} = log flushed, not data pages",
                "{blue:Redo log}: replays committed changes lost from memory",
                "{red:Undo log}: rolls back uncommitted changes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Checkpoints",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==checkpoint== flushes dirty pages and records a **log position**",
                "Crash recovery starts there, not at the start of the log"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Crash",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Last checkpoint",
                    "sub": "start here",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redo",
                    "sub": "committed work",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Undo",
                    "sub": "uncommitted work",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Point-in-Time Recovery",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==PITR== = restore a **base backup**, then replay archived WAL/binlog",
                "Stop at a target timestamp or LSN, just before the bad statement",
                "PostgreSQL: `archive_command` ships WAL; set the target, add `recovery.signal`, start"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "archive_command = 'cp %p /archive/%f'",
                "# restore base backup, then in postgresql.conf:",
                "recovery_target_time = '2026-10-28 14:05:00'",
                "touch $PGDATA/recovery.signal"
              ],
              "note": "start the server; it replays WAL up to the target"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "WAL archiving was not enabled **before** the incident, so there is nothing to replay and ==PITR is impossible==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ARIES Crash Recovery Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ARIES Crash Recovery Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Principles and LSNs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Write-ahead logging==: log reaches disk before the data page",
                "==Repeat history== during redo, even for losers",
                "Undo is logged too, as ==CLRs== (compensation log records)",
                "Every log record has an ==LSN==; each page stores its `pageLSN`",
                "Redo skips a record when `pageLSN >= LSN`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Buffer policy",
                "Meaning",
                "Needs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Steal**",
                  "Dirty pages of uncommitted txns may reach disk",
                  "{red:Undo}"
                ],
                [
                  "**No-force**",
                  "Commit does not force pages to disk",
                  "{blue:Redo}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Checkpoint and Three Passes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Fuzzy checkpoint== saves the dirty page table and transaction table",
                "Transactions keep running while it is taken"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Analysis",
                    "sub": "rebuild dirty pages + active txns from checkpoint",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redo",
                    "sub": "replay from earliest recLSN, losers too",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Undo",
                    "sub": "roll back losers, write CLRs",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Redo is not committed-only",
              "text": "ARIES redoes ==all history== first, losers included, and only then undoes the uncommitted transactions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Replication for High Availability",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Replication for High Availability",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Primary-Replica Replication",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Primary ==ships its WAL / binlog== to every replica",
                "Replicas serve **reads**",
                "A replica can be ==promoted== if the primary fails"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Synchronous vs Asynchronous",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Synchronous",
                "Asynchronous"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Commit",
                  "waits for replica ack",
                  "returns at once"
                ],
                [
                  "Data loss",
                  "{green:zero}",
                  "{red:recent commits lost}"
                ],
                [
                  "Latency",
                  "higher",
                  "low"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "slow commits",
                  "**replication lag** on failover"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Failover Steps",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Detect",
                    "note": "primary is down",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Promote",
                    "note": "most up-to-date replica",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repoint",
                    "note": "clients to new primary",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fence",
                    "note": "old primary, avoids split-brain",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Replication is not a backup",
              "text": "A `DROP TABLE` or bad `UPDATE` hits ==every replica immediately==. You still need **PITR** and backups."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Never restore-testing backups or rehearsing failover",
                "==An untested backup is not a backup=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Access Control: GRANT, REVOKE, Roles and Row-Level Security",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Access Control: GRANT, REVOKE, Roles and Row-Level Security",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. GRANT, REVOKE, Roles",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`WITH GRANT OPTION` lets grantees delegate: only when truly needed",
                "Roles bundle privileges; ==users get roles==, not direct grants"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON orders TO analyst;",
                "REVOKE INSERT ON orders FROM analyst;",
                "CREATE ROLE readonly;",
                "GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA app TO readonly;",
                "GRANT readonly TO alice;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Least Privilege",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each app gets its own role with ==only the needed rights==",
                "Never run the app as the **owner** or a superuser",
                "Revoke default ==PUBLIC== privileges"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Row-Level Security",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Enable RLS on the table, then add a policy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "ALTER TABLE docs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;",
                "CREATE POLICY own_rows ON docs USING (owner = current_user);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "No policy",
                  "non-owners see ==zero rows== (default deny)"
                ],
                [
                  "Owner, superuser",
                  "bypass RLS unless `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`"
                ],
                [
                  "Writes",
                  "controlled by `WITH CHECK`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "REVOKE gotcha",
              "text": "REVOKE on a role does not remove privileges inherited through another role or granted to ==PUBLIC==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
